{"id":"v12","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":14,"of":15,"title":"The preposition the verb wants","titleHe":"פֹּעַל וּמִלַּת יַחַס","goal":"Learn verbs together with the preposition they take — because it is rarely English's.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"A Hebrew verb usually arrives welded to one particular preposition, and knowing the verb without it gets you a sentence nobody says. You do not wait to someone in English, but Hebrew waits לְ. Learn the pair as one item."},{"type":"table","caption":"Verbs and their prepositions","head":["English","Hebrew"],"rows":[["to help someone","עָזַר לְ־"],["to wait for","חִכָּה לְ־"],["to answer someone","עָנָה לְ־"],["to look at","הִסְתַּכֵּל עַל"],["to tell about","סִפֵּר עַל"],["to give up on","וִתֵּר עַל"],["to ask someone for","בִּקֵּשׁ מִ־"],["to use","הִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּ־"],["to believe in","הֶאֱמִין בְּ־"],["to be interested in","הִתְעַנְיֵן בְּ־"],["to go into","נִכְנַס לְ־"],["to go out of","יָצָא מִ־"],["to get married to","הִתְחַתֵּן עִם"],["to meet someone","פָּגַשׁ אֶת"]]},{"type":"text","body":"Once the preposition is chosen, it declines: whatever pronoun follows the verb is fused onto the preposition rather than standing on its own."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"חִכִּיתִי לוֹ שָׁעָה.","en":"I waited an hour for him."},{"he":"הִיא עָזְרָה לִי מְאוֹד.","en":"She helped me a great deal."},{"he":"הִסְתַּכַּלְתִּי עָלֶיהָ.","en":"I looked at her."},{"he":"הִשְׁתַּמַּשְׁתִּי בּוֹ.","en":"I used it."},{"he":"סִפַּרְתִּי לָהֶם עַל הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"I told them about the book."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"That last example carries both at once: סִפֵּר takes לְ for the person told and עַל for the thing told about. Verbs with two prepositions are common, and the order is fixed — person first."},{"type":"tip","body":"A dictionary entry that reads עָזַר לְ־ is not being sloppy about where the entry ends. The dash is the entry. Copy it into your notes with the preposition attached and you will never have to unlearn it."}],"vocab":[{"he":"עָזַר לְ","en":"helped (someone)","translit":"azar le"},{"he":"חִכָּה לְ","en":"waited for","translit":"chika le"},{"he":"הִסְתַּכֵּל עַל","en":"looked at","translit":"histakel al"},{"he":"הִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּ","en":"used","translit":"hishtamesh be"},{"he":"הֶאֱמִין בְּ","en":"believed in","translit":"he'emin be"},{"he":"וִתֵּר עַל","en":"gave up on","translit":"viter al"},{"he":"הִתְחַתֵּן עִם","en":"married","translit":"hitchaten im"},{"he":"הִתְעַנְיֵן בְּ","en":"took an interest in","translit":"hit'anyen be"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["meal","sees","helped (someone)","night"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עָזַר לְ","translit":"azar le"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["stomach, belly","husband","childhood","waited for"],"correct":3,"prompt":"חִכָּה לְ","translit":"chika le"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["pencil","looked at","maybe","that is to say (כלומר)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הִסְתַּכֵּל עַל","translit":"histakel al"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["old man, elder","garden","used","believed in"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּ","translit":"hishtamesh be"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["remembers","hat","believed in","to go"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הֶאֱמִין בְּ","translit":"he'emin be"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["blessing","truth","accepted, customary","gave up on"],"correct":3,"prompt":"וִתֵּר עַל","translit":"viter al"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["slowly","watch, clock","married","palm frond"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הִתְחַתֵּן עִם","translit":"hitchaten im"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “waited for”?","options":["בְּרָכָה","חִכָּה לְ","כָּבוֹד","עָזַר לְ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["עָזַר לְ","helped (someone)"],["חִכָּה לְ","waited for"],["הִסְתַּכֵּל עַל","looked at"],["הִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּ","used"],["הֶאֱמִין בְּ","believed in"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “gave up on”?","options":["אָהוּב","חֹדֶשׁ","וִתֵּר עַל","מָלֵא"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___ לָהֶם עַל הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"I told them about the book.","options":["הֶאֱמִין בְּ","הִסְתַּכֵּל עַל","וִתֵּר עַל","סִפַּרְתִּי"],"correct":3,"full":"סִפַּרְתִּי לָהֶם עַל הַסֵּפֶר."},{"type":"choice","q":"Verbs and their prepositions — to be interested in?","options":["עָנָה לְ־","חִכָּה לְ־","הִתְעַנְיֵן בְּ־","עָזַר לְ־"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"הִתְחַתֵּן עִם","translit":"hitchaten im","en":"married"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["הִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּ","עָזַר לְ","חִכָּה לְ","וִתֵּר עַל"],"correct":1,"say":"עָזַר לְ","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Verbs and their prepositions — to give up on?","options":["עָנָה לְ־","חִכָּה לְ־","עָזַר לְ־","וִתֵּר עַל"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “waited for” in Hebrew","answer":"חִכָּה לְ","hint":"chika le"}]}